 ## 2026-07-20
 
+### 1528 — Relay binding frozen on interface-first accepted foundations (TASK-260715-111tde)
+- OVERRIDE / ROUTING: The reviewer-accepted task override supersedes the 1510 stop-line and deliberately decouples this reusable wire contract from Gate A0 and TASK-260715-32umrc. Binding authority is the accepted ReluxTunnelCore boundary (TASK-260715-2nfz7w), cgo-free Go 1.26.5 relay toolchain (TASK-260715-3bdplx), candidate-neutral SSHExecChannel (TASK-260720-100wu6), and ADR-005/006. The obsolete A0/32umrc dependency edges are removed; those decisions remain outside the relay contract.
+- DECISION: Canonical JSON at `Protocol/Relay/relay-v1.schema.json` generates checked-in Swift/Go values only; handwritten Swift in `ReluxTunnelCore/RelayProtocol` and Go in `relay/internal/protocol` own behavior. `make relay-protocol-generate` is the sole regeneration command and `make relay-protocol-check` owns deterministic double-generation, drift/manual-edit failure, compilation, and schema-negative gates. No Swift/Go FFI or runtime schema parser is permitted.
+- DECISION: Build identity uses a separate bounded `relux-relay --identity --protocol 1` exec record matched to the signed manifest before `--stdio --protocol 1`; the fixed 12/16-byte v1 hello remains unchanged and framed stdout stays uncontaminated. DNS priority is a negotiated scheduling hint only. HEV `MSGLEN` is DATA length, `HDRLEN` includes the three-byte prefix, and domain wire length is capped at 248 by one-byte `HDRLEN`.
+- RESIDUAL: TASK-260715-18owh7 remains the sole unblocked owner of association/queue/datagram/idle numeric values and their compatibility-safe v1 exchange or local-cap policy. No values were invented and no duplicate blocker was created.
+- VERIFICATION: The binding record, ownership component source, and session-establishment sequence source are task-scoped outcomes. PlantUML 1.2026.6 validates and renders both through internal Smetana layout; the workstation Graphviz `dot` still lacks `libltdl.7.dylib`, so the diagram workflow does not rely on it.
+
 ### 1510 — Relay binding stopped on unaccepted Gate A0 and project architecture (TASK-260715-111tde)
 - STOP-THE-LINE: The required foundation outcomes are not accepted: TASK-260715-1828xy is backlog/blocked with no Gate A0 ADR, and TASK-260715-32umrc is backlog/blocked with only a planning diagram and no generated-project architecture ADR. Freezing protocol schema placement, generated/source ownership, or production module boundaries would invent the viability and target-ownership decisions forbidden by the task handoff.
 - ANOMALY / ROUTING: TASK-260715-111tde was allowed into analysis while its board graph named only the already-done TASK-260715-2nfz7w as a blocker; the two prerequisites existed only in a precondition resource. Direct dependencies on TASK-260715-1828xy and TASK-260715-32umrc are now linked, including the resulting parent escalation.
